2. NASA Valkyrie robot model (val_description)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) NASA Johnson Space Center Robotics.
Original source: https://github.com/NASA-JSC-Robotics/val_description
Licensed under the NASA Open Source Agreement (NOSA) Version 1.3.

The original NASA copyright is retained. In accordance with NOSA v1.3, this
NOTICE states that the NASA Valkyrie description has been MODIFIED here for
use in the MuJoCo / mjlab simulator. Summary of modifications:

  - Converted 75 Collada (.dae) visual meshes to Wavefront OBJ (MuJoCo does
    not load Collada).
  - Preprocessed the URDF: removed Gazebo plugin, transmission, and sensor
    tags; welded the 26 finger joints and the Hokuyo laser joint (fixed),
    which are not used for locomotion.
  - Rebuilt a clean MJCF (MuJoCo XML) via mjSpec: added a free-joint floating
    base at the pelvis, set visual geoms to render-only, enabled feet-only
    collision geometry, added foot sites and a pelvis IMU site with five
    sensors, and corrected degenerate sensor-frame inertials.
  - Added actuators (PD position control) and a crouch-stand keyframe.

These modifications are distributed under the same NOSA v1.3 terms as the
original. No claim is made to the underlying NASA Valkyrie design; only the
integration work is the contribution of this fork's author.

The MJCF and meshes under `src/mjlab/asset_zoo/robots/nasa_valkyrie/xmls/`
are derived from NASA's val_description and remain subject to NOSA v1.3.
